889" 13194139536004 17592186045443 true] [17592186556057 1074 "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/59/59dd651e6e27665841463b1d6f8f8409801ca6bd5f15428e2cb5cf65328a2528.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 21.1\\cdot 22.1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56.4}^{∘} \\\\  & =233.155\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56.4}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈194.199\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 24.2\\cdot 16.7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56.4}^{∘} \\\\  & =202.07\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{56.4}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈168.308\\,4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈194.199\\,8+168.308\\,4 \\\\  & ≈362.508\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest tenth, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $362.5.$" 13194139536004 17592186045443 true] [17592186556058 1080 "15.0" 13194139536004 17592186045443 true] [17592186556058 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536004 17592186045443 true] [17592186556058 1083 #uuid "224d4162-73d4-507d-9dff-d0df11cad464" 13194139536004 17592186045443 true] [17592186556059 1075 #edb/ref 17592186556078 13194139536004 17592186045443 true] [17592186556059 1075 #edb/ref 17592186556088 13194139536004 17592186045443 true] [17592186556059 1075 #edb/ref 17592186556089 13194139536004 17592186045443 true] [17592186556059 1075 #edb/ref 17592186556093 13194139536004 17592186045443 true] [17592186556059 1075 #edb/ref 17592186556098 13194139536004 17592186045443 true] [17592186556059 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139536004 17592186045443 true] [17592186556059 1077 "selection" 13194139536004 17592186045443 true] [17592186556059 1078 